## What this track proposes

The track plans and accepts the civic group of scene blueprints. It claims all 32 civic rows in
the 100-scene list. Two rows, blacksmith-shop and tavern, are already accepted at 7.5; the other
30 are mockup-needed. The track will reconcile existing mockups and scene sources, pick a next
scene, define shared fit rules, assemble one scene from catalog assets, compare renders with the
mockup, and refresh the blueprint status.

## How the current system works, per this spec

The file docs/fantasy-world-scene-blueprints.tsv holds one row per scene with a group, priority,
and status. Two civic rows are accepted and 30 are mockup-needed. Two civic scene sources exist
at scenes/blacksmith-shop.ts and scenes/tavern-interior.ts with comparison renders in
docs/blacksmith-mockups/ and docs/tavern-mockups/. The fit sheet docs/dungeon-mockups/fit-check.md
fixes dungeon verticals for a 1.0 m character. The catalog docs/fantasy-world-asset-catalog.md
defines asset IDs, and the rubric in review.md scores assets out of 10 with a priority-based bar.
Mockups need image generation, and paid generation needs PM approval.

